 do to  change well the first thing I did was to  be absolutely clear about things like  anti-semitism and that's why i issued an  apology in my acceptance speech the  first opportunity that I had to our  Jewish communities and that's why I've  already had meetings with Jewish leaders  in the past week so absolutely  demonstrating change I then put together  a very talented diverse shadow cabinet  from across the whole of United Kingdom  to demonstrate that we've got the  strength and talent in depth across the  labour party to take us forward  obviously where we go next is now framed  by coronavirus because the arguments  about our economy are going to be  different and the argue and the  arguments about how we value people  frankly are going to be different we  can't go out every Thursday on our  doorsteps and clap for our key workers  who are keeping us going in this period  and then at the end of this return to  business as usual so the job of the  Labour Party is to spell out that vision  of a better society when we're through  coronavirus but ok well let's talk a bit  about that vision because you're right  of course to say that all of the old  certainties are going to be ripped up  because of coronavirus and there's going  to be a crippling economic cost as well  you've said that you can't have another  decade of austerity but there will be  austerity won't there of some form  that's the reality because we'll be  paying us off for a generation what  there are choices about how you deal  with debt and deficit and the government  this government going back to 2010 for  the last decade has chosen austerity  that is that has caused great harm to  many communities and many individuals  across the United Kingdom what we can't  have is another decade of austerity on  top of this decade of austerity just  look what it's done to the health  service our public services social care  all of these areas for 10 years what  would you do instead then would you  raise taxes rather than cuts down  spending  well we we may well have to raise taxes  of course but you're asking me a  question that nobody can realistically  answer because we don't yet know what  the damage the economy is going to be we  do know it's going to be damaged we can  see that already we don't know because  we don't know how long this is going to  go on quite what the damage will be so  pretending now that I can tell you what  will be needed in 2024 is not something  that I'm going to do but it is clear  that we're going to have to take a  different approach lots of people who  are key workers today going in today as  they've been going in every day have  been underpaid and undervalued for years  that cannot go on there's got to be a  fundamental difference going forward  okay now you completed your shadow  cabinet reshuffle last week and you  booted out quite a lot of jeremy  corbyn's old allies which a burger and  dom butler john tricky in Lavery john  macdonald Diane Abbott have left the  stage I got the sense when I last  interviewed Jeremy Corbyn that he was  angling for a job in the shadow cabinet  that wasn't forthcoming either is this  the end of Corbin ISM well I've never  accepted these labels based on an  individual what I'm trying to do is  build a team a diverse team from  different parts of the party across the  country that can take us on the journey  from here to where we need to be at the  next general election and what I said in  my election campaign and what I say to  my top team now is don't look to the  Past for people to cling to we've got to  do the thinking here we've got to build  the policy build and the project build  and and the strategy to take us into the  next general election so that the the  duty and responsibility is on us now to  do what's necessary over the next four  years not not to to look backward to  other individuals whoever they may be a  key part of the Jeremy Corbyn project as  well was the campaign group momentum who  really backed his leadership to the hilt  when you were elected they tweeted to  say in this new era momentum will play a  new role will hold Kier to account and  make sure he keeps his promises and on  the show last week Anne  Allen Johnson referenced that tweet and  said to me I'm afraid there's no sign  they'd borrowed the weapons and have  dedicated themselves to unity and as a  result labor under your leadership needs  to purge ourselves of the far-left  insurgents of momentum is he right  look what I've said to our membership is  this whether you voted for me or not I  will represent you I will listen to you  and I'll bring our party together I want  to hear all the voices in the Labor  Party of course I should be held to  account for what I've said and what I do  of course I should that's absolutely  right but what I want to do is to unify  our party we've got five hundred and  eighty thousand members that's the  biggest political party in Europe we  need to pull that together as a really  strong fighting force so I will talk to  everybody within our party about how we  do that okay and just finally I'm  running out of time I'm quite interested  to find a bit more about yourself that  new leader the Labour Party blank canvas  big mandate to do what you want  now you went from Grammar School to  Oxford you then became Director of  Public Prosecutions head of the CPS  electors as an MP in 2015 five years  later you're leading the Labour Party's  a very impressive CV it's also quite an  establishment CCB though do you think  some people may feel it's time for an  insurgent well along the way I've been a  human rights lawyer fighting cases  across the world against governments and  the establishment as you put it so I  don't buy into this you're either the  establishment or you're not well I  focused on is what needs to get done and  how do I get it done but I've spent many  many years fighting the establishment as  you put it whether that's for trade  unionists or that's people on but on  death row across the world you name it  I've been there fighting on the front  line with them of course I've also  worked in the Crown Prosecution Service  I also work with the police service in  Northern Ireland on some of implementing  some of the Good Friday proposals and  what I focused on is not am I the  establishment or not the establishment  what's the job that needs to be done  what's the the wrong that needs to be  right  and that's the focus I will take leading  the Labour Party which is how do we get  the Labour Party a most incredible force  for good from where it is now into a  position where we can serve our country  again in government okay  thank you very much on the program this  morning kissed on about a new leader of  Labour Party
 

